|Strings |
|--------|
-A string is simply a sequence of characters (text data).
-Strings are immutable.
-Python allows 4 ways to define strings, they are

  1. By using Single Quotes
    -Use for simple Text
    Ex: s1 = ‘AVD Group’
  2. By using Double Quotes
    -Use double quotes When your text contains single quotes inside
    Ex: s1 = “It’s Good Day”
  3. By using Triple single Quotes
    -Use for multi-line Strings
    Ex: data = '''101,siva,50000
                102,kiran,60000'''
        print(data)
  4. By using Triple Double Quotes
     Use when you want to create document strings
    Ex:
      log = """ERROR: Disk full
            Time: 10:30PM """
      print(log)

